SUMMARY:LFS Feminist Consciousness-Raising Film Afternoons
DESCRIPTION:Lancaster Freethought Society\n**Feminist Film Afternoons #2: 
 Salt of the Earth (1954)**\n**What happens when women discover that fighti
 ng for their families isn't enough—they must fight for their own equalit
 y\, too?**\nJoin us for the second of five Feminist Consciousness-Raising 
 Film Afternoons\, featuring *Salt of the Earth*\, a groundbreaking America
 n film based on a real miners' strike in New Mexico.\nWhen Mexican-America
 n miners strike against dangerous working conditions and discriminatory wa
 ges\, a court injunction prevents the men from picketing. Their wives step
  forward to take their places\, while the men must assume responsibility f
 or the households and children.\nWhat begins as support for their husbands
  becomes something much more powerful: women discovering their own politic
 al agency.\n\n**After the film\, we'll discuss:**\n\n* How did the women's
  understanding of their own oppression change through collective action?\n
 * What happened when men and women exchanged their traditional responsibil
 ities?\n* Can a movement for equality succeed if women remain subordinate 
 within that movement?\n\nThis is a relaxed\, friendly afternoon of film an
 d conversation—not a lecture or debate. Everyone is welcome to share the
 ir experiences and perspectives.\n\n**The Details**\n\n* **When:** Sunday\
 , November 29\, 2–5 PM\n* **Where:** Private home in Millersville. Addre
 ss provided individually to confirmed attendees.\n* **Seating:** Limited t
 o six guests.\n* **Attendance:** Women have priority through Saturday. If 
 spaces remain\, men may RSVP beginning Saturday\, November 28 at noon.\n* 
 **Guests:** No additional guests\, please.\n\nEach film afternoon stands o
 n its own. Come to one or several—no preparation or ongoing commitment r
 equired.\n**Bring your curiosity\, your ideas\, and your willingness to im
 agine something better!**
